    "open_questions": [
      "Read Rhythmic Composition (Hudson, 2014): Branam's published transcriptions of twenty Porcupine Tree parts would settle the leads from tabs (Harridan's threes, Futile's dotted eighths, Anesthetize's 3+3+2) and replace the Songsterr bars.",
      "Locate a displacement and a metric modulation on a named record, with its ratio; the books and interviews give the method, not the bar.",
      "The Start of Something Beautiful: he describes 9/8 and 5/8; the tab writes the verse in 5/4. Which it is on the record.",
      "Write Futile and Way Out of Here: their 7/8 and 6/8 are in sixteenths, and the eighth meters hold eighths."
    ]
  },
